/*!
    \qmltype notarization
    \inqmlmodule QbsModules
    \since Qbs 3.5

    \brief Provides support for notarizing macOS distributables.

    The \c notarization module provides properties for submitting signed macOS application
    bundles, disk images, and other distributables to Apple's notary service and stapling the
    resulting ticket. When \l{notarization::enableNotarization}{enableNotarization} is \c true,
    notarization is performed automatically as part of the \l{bundle} and \l{dmg} build steps,
    similar to how the \l{codesign} module integrates with those modules.

    This module is only available when building for Apple platforms on a macOS host.

    Notarization requires artifacts to be signed beforehand with a \c Developer ID Application
    certificate. Use the \l{codesign} module with \l{codesign::signingType}{codesign.signingType}
    set to \c{"apple-id"} and enable the hardened runtime via
    \l{codesign::codesignFlags}{codesign.codesignFlags}.

    Credentials for Apple's notary service are separate from code signing certificates. Authenticate
    with a keychain profile created with \c{notarytool store-credentials}. \c notarytool reads the
    Apple ID, app-specific password, and team ID from that profile, so the password is not stored
    in the build graph.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty bool notarization::enableNotarization

    Whether to notarize distributable macOS artifacts produced by this product.

    \defaultvalue \c false
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty string notarization::notarytoolPath

    The path to the \c notarytool binary.

    \defaultvalue \c notarytool from \c{PATH}, or \c xcrun if \c notarytool is not found
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty string notarization::staplerPath

    The path to the \c stapler binary.

    \defaultvalue \c stapler from \c{PATH}, or \c xcrun if \c stapler is not found
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty string notarization::keychainProfile

    The name of the keychain profile created with \c{notarytool store-credentials}.

    \c notarytool reads the Apple ID, app-specific password, and team ID from this profile.
    \QBS passes only the profile name.

    This value is specific to the build machine. Set it in a
    \l{Configuring Profiles and Preferences}{profile}.
    It is required when \l{notarization::enableNotarization}{enableNotarization} is \c true.

    \nodefaultvalue
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty bool notarization::staple

    Whether to run \c{stapler staple} after successful notarization.

    \defaultvalue \c true
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty stringList notarization::notarytoolFlags

    Additional command-line flags passed to \c{notarytool submit}.

    \nodefaultvalue
*/
